---
title: ":microbe: Amish Friendship Bread Starter"
source: https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/7063/amish-friendship-bread-starter/
serves: 4
prep time: 30 minutes
total time: 10 days
tags:
  - ingredient
  - sourdough
  - starter
  - allrecipes
---

Dissolve @active dry yeast{1%package} (0.25 oz) in @warm water{0.25%cup} (110°F / 45°C) in a #small bowl{}. Let stand until foamy, about ~{10%minutes}.

Day 1: Combine @all-purpose flour{1%cup} and @granulated sugar{1%cup} in a non-metal 2-quart #larger container{} (glass, plastic, or ceramic) and mix thoroughly. Stir in @milk{1%cup} and the foamy yeast mixture using a #wooden spoon{}. Cover the container loosely and leave at room temperature until bubbly.

Days 2 through 4: Stir the starter daily with a #wooden spoon{}.

Day 5: Stir in @all-purpose flour{1%cup}, @granulated sugar{1%cup}, and @milk{1%cup}.

Days 6 through 9: Stir the starter daily with a #wooden spoon{}.

Day 10: Stir in the remaining @all-purpose flour{1%cup}, @granulated sugar{1%cup}, and @milk{1%cup}. Remove 1 cup starter to bake your first batch of bread. Give 2 cups starter to friends (1 cup each) along with this recipe and your favorite Amish bread recipe. Store the remaining 1 cup starter in a container in the refrigerator or begin the 10-day cycle again starting at Day 2.
